@startuml
' Figure 45.5  Guarded text-to-SQL
' Reading order: top to bottom. The analyst's question becomes a typed
' metric request; the semantic layer compiles it and the row policy
' checks the requester's role before any SQL runs; raw SQL from the
' agent is refused; the answer names its metric version.
' From designs/internal_specs/lakeshore-analytics.toml.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
participant "Analyst" as U <<org>>
participant "Agent" as A <<knowledge>>
participant "Semantic layer" as S <<knowledge>>
participant "Row policy" as P <<policy>>
U -> A : Question
A -> S : Metric request
S -> P : Requester's role
P -> S : Allowed rows
S -> A : Value, version
A -[$POLICY]> S : Raw SQL
S -[$POLICY]> A : Refused
A -> U : Answer, source
@enduml
